obsd-mcp is a read-only Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that lets an AI
agent inspect the OpenBSD base system: system overview, network state,
allowlisted /etc config files with secrets redacted, and optional pf,
unbound and bgpd status.

It is sandboxed with unveil(2) and pledge(2), runs only fixed base-system
commands without a shell, refuses to run as root, and has no tools that
write files or change system state. It speaks MCP over stdio; use an
ssh(1) forced command for remote access.

The server binary is installed as /usr/local/libexec/obsd-mcp.
